
  <sn><md>## Set up C in Linux

Setting up C for development on Linux is typically **straightforward**, as the `necessary tools are readily available through your distribution's package manager`. The most common approach is to install the **GNU Compiler Collection** (GCC).

Here is a step-by-step guide to get you started:
</md></sn>
